From fe172bcc19f66e8e7416230ce2430f4cb799b0f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kshot3000 <kshot9000@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 21:52:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix stale pending-outgoing UTXO lock, 24h change reference,
 auth fail-closed, address validation

- pending-outgoing: inputs of never-confirmed (>48h stale) broadcast records
  were permanently excluded from availableUtxos, locking funds in the send
  preview and available-balance display. Staleness is now checked before
  marking inputs spent; regression tests added.
- server: /api/safetrade 24h changePercent measured against the first trade
  inside the window (could span minutes on low-volume pairs). Now uses the
  last trade before the window (priorTrade), extracted to stats24h() in
  market.mjs with tests.
- server: /api/safetrade auth now fails closed when PEARL_READ_TOKEN is unset
  (previously a missing token silently disabled auth).
- keystore: encryptMnemonic address check hardened from startsWith('prl1p')
  to full isValidPearlAddress() for the AES-GCM AAD binding.
- Promoted the taproot-signing consensus check to a permanent regression test
  (signatures verify against the tweaked output key).
